CLUB: SOCIETY OF MIDWEST CONTESTERS
CREATED-BY: N1MM Logger+ 1.0.10822.0
SOAPBOX: Intended full time operation but pulled the plug the first night after operating just 1 Hour 45 minutes as I was so disappointed in the band conditions. Got an attitude readjustment Saturday morning and then put in a pretty fulltime effort the second night. Heard no Europeans but kept searching for KH6AQ the second night and easily worked them (working them under such bad conditions was gratifying and they apparently have great ears). Once again used my Kenwood TS-180s which will turn 46 years old in 4 days from now accompanied by a Hi-Per Mite active audio filter (200 Hz bandwidth). TX antenna 68 foot base loaded vertical with 55 short buried radials (2500 feet of radials), and 3 half size pennant antennas for receive pointed (40, 160, and 300 degrees). 160 meters has been my favorite band for many years and I really enjoy the 160 meter CW contests above all other contests. Thanks to everyone that operated the contest, and it sure was great working so many of my Topband friends..
SOAPBOX: 73,
SOAPBOX: Don (wd8dsb)
